        "title": "Add weekly session-equivalent headroom",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- estimate remaining weekly quota as full 5-hour windows from the median burn across the latest seven completed active session windows\n- show the estimate verdict first, then the numeric headroom line, only after at least three reliable samples\n- support Codex, Claude, Antigravity/Gemini, and generic providers with unambiguous session/weekly pairs\n- respect weekly work-day settings, isolate provider/account/window history, and memoize the existing history scan\n- localize the new pluralized output and accessibility labels across all 23 catalogs\n\nAddresses #2261. The issue remains open for reporter confirmation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `swift test --filter SessionEquivalentForecastTests` — 23 tests passed\n- `swift test --filter 'SessionEquivalentForecastTests|UsageStorePlanUtilizationTests'` — 101 tests passed\n- source-blind behavior contract — 19 feature cases passed\n- `make check` — SwiftFormat, SwiftLint, localization, docs, scripts, and repository gates passed\n- all 23 stringsdict catalogs passed `plutil -lint`\n- full sharded suite on the feature head before the final isolation hardening — 700 selections passed; exact-head CI is the final full-suite gate\n- repeated branch autoreview; all accepted findings fixed, including named-window isolation and preservation of generic weekly reset/history behavior\n\n## Presentation\n\nVerdict leads; numeric estimate follows. The reporter has not answered the ordering question yet, so this uses the owner-approved default.\n",
